Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `h.res` was consumed by the move `^h.res`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/resource_move_needs_mark.jet:63:17
    |
 63 |     print(h.res.name)
    |                 ^^^^
  --> tests/ui/resource_move_needs_mark.jet:62:16
    |
 62 |     out :: Val(^h.res)
    |                ^^^^^^ `h.res` moved to the move `^h.res` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `h.res` after the move, or give the move `^h.res` a copy with `h.res.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121

